{
  "_description": "dirty-claude patch table. SAME pipeline as godClaude (extract cli.js -> patch_cli.py applies these -> bun build --compile), but this is a CONTROL project, not a prompt-patch project: the 66 prompt/anti-slop patches were removed. Add control-channel injection patches here.",
  "_source": "Copied 1:1 from godClaude tools/bundle/extract-recompile/, then emptied of prompt patches — the only intended difference between the two repos.",
  "_versioning": "Anchor patches on invariant content (OTel event names, API field names, prompt prose), never minified names — every internal name (dA5, w1) changes each Claude release.",
  "_anchor_strategy": "Each patch matches `old` (a unique anchor in cli.js) and replaces with `new`. An `id` starting with INJECT@ inserts `new` BEFORE the anchor (anchor preserved) — use for code injection. `resolve: true` uses anchor_template/replacement_template with {{symbol}} placeholders resolved from stable anchors at build time. See patch_cli.py.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "id": "INJECT@dirty_control_channel",
      "_what": "Inject the dirty-claude control-channel useEffect into Claude's main REPL. Wraps globalThis.fetch (idempotent via __dc_fetch_wrapped) to tee every api.anthropic.com response via ReadableStream.tee() — branch A flows untouched to Claude, branch B drains per-chunk into __dc_http_log AND emits each chunk to all SSE subscribers in real time. Scans the accumulated stream for the Anthropic `stop_reason` field and broadcasts `event: turn.end` when the value is terminal (end_turn / max_tokens / stop_sequence / refusal); tool_use / pause_turn keep the stream open for the follow-up call. Boots a localhost node:http server on $DC_PORT (default 47291) with: GET /v1/state, POST /v1/answer (race-safe via __dc_dialog_cache), GET /v1/stream (ambient SSE subscriber), and POST /v1/prompt with content-negotiation — `Accept: application/json` keeps the blocking JSON behavior (full httpResponses[]+messages[] payload), `Accept: text/event-stream` opens an SSE response and forwards every chunk in real time, closing on turn.end. Dialog transitions (l6 setter activity) broadcast as dialog.opened / dialog.closed events.",
      "_anchor_strategy": "Anchor is the start of the I1 useCallback declaration in the main REPL component, right after `X74({executeQueuedInput:kCH,...})`. By this point kCH, R4, l6, j6, AH are all declared, so the injected useEffect can capture them safely (no TDZ). INJECT inserts a fresh useEffect BEFORE this anchor — fires on mount and on l6 transitions (deps=[kCH,R4,l6]), wraps fetch once, boots HTTP server once. Anchor stays unique on minify; kCH/R4/l6/j6/AH references in `new` are minified names pinned to 2.1.150 — fail-closed on rename, re-paste manually.",
      "_caveats": "(1) Single-process, localhost-only — singleton enforced by tools/run.sh. (2) SSE turn.end is signal-based (stop_reason scan) with a DC_STABLE_MS idle fallback for slash-command paths that never hit api.anthropic.com. (3) No subscriber filtering in phase 1: SSE subscribers receive ALL broadcast events including ambient terminal-user activity. Client filters by turn_uuid if needed. (4) lastStopReason is per-fetch-call (declared inside the drain IIFE) so concurrent Anthropic calls don't clobber each other; the regex scans the accumulated TX with a 30-byte overlap so chunk-boundary splits don't miss the field. (5) __dc_http_log ring buffer cap=200. (6) No auth. (7) Body decoded as UTF-8 — binary lossy (anthropic is JSON/SSE, fine in practice). (8) HTTP submit path goes through kCH queue-drainer (same convergence at j74 — hooks + slash parser still fire).",
      "_source": "Body lives in sources/dirty_control_channel.js (readable, ~370 lines). Inlined into `new` field by inline_sources.py before patch_cli.py runs. Re-run inline_sources.py after editing the .js file; patches.json is the canonical artifact patch_cli.py reads.",
      "old": "let I1=f6.useCallback(async(v_,z6)=>{",
      "new_source": "dirty_control_channel.js",
      "new": "// dirty-claude control channel — INJECT@dirty_control_channel\n//\n// Source-of-truth (readable). Inlined into patches.json's \"new\" field by\n// tools/pipeline/inline_sources.py before patch_cli.py runs.\n//\n// What changed vs prior version: real-time SSE streaming. Anthropic SSE\n// chunks are forwarded per-chunk to subscribers (zero extra latency vs the\n// upstream stream), turn boundaries detected from \"stop_reason\" field\n// (no more DC_STABLE_MS heuristic for the streaming path), dialog\n// transitions broadcast as events. Blocking JSON path on POST /v1/prompt\n// preserved bit-for-bit for backward compat.\n//\n// Endpoints:\n//   POST /v1/prompt\n//     Accept: application/json (default) -> blocking, returns full JSON\n//     Accept: text/event-stream          -> SSE, per-chunk events, closes on turn.end\n//   GET  /v1/stream                      -> ambient SSE subscriber, never closes\n//   GET  /v1/state                       -> unchanged\n//   POST /v1/answer                      -> unchanged\n//\n// Event schema (sent to all SSE subscribers):\n//   event: turn.start        data: {turn_uuid, prompt}        (POST SSE only, one-shot)\n//   event: anthropic.chunk   data: {url, chunk}               (every Anthropic SSE chunk)\n//   event: dialog.opened     data: {dialog_id, component, propKeys}\n//   event: dialog.closed     data: {dialog_id}\n//   event: turn.end          data: {stop_reason, source, url?} (terminal stop_reason or idle fallback)\n//   :ping                                                     (keep-alive every 15s)\n//\n// Design notes — see docs/control-channel.md for full doc.\n//   1. lastStopReason is PER-FETCH-CALL (declared inside IIFE), not global,\n//      so concurrent Anthropic calls don't clobber each other.\n//   2. stop_reason regex runs on accumulated TX (with -30 byte overlap on\n//      the new region), so chunk-boundary splits don't miss the field.\n//   3. No subscriber filtering in phase 1. SSE subscribers receive ALL\n//      broadcast events including ambient terminal-user activity. Caveat\n//      documented; promote to filter-by-turn_uuid if real pain emerges.\n//   4. broadcast() and subscriber Set live on globalThis; fetch wrap and\n//      dialog detection read them via globalThis lazily so React re-renders\n//      don't capture stale references.\n\nf6.useEffect(() => {\n  // ========== One-time install (fetch wrap + broadcast + subscriber Set) ==========\n  if (!globalThis.__dc_fetch_wrapped) {\n    globalThis.__dc_fetch_wrapped = true;\n    globalThis.__dc_http_log = [];\n    globalThis.__dc_subscribers = globalThis.__dc_subscribers || new Set();\n    globalThis.__dc_TURN_END_REASONS = new Set([\"end_turn\", \"max_tokens\", \"stop_sequence\", \"refusal\"]);\n    globalThis.__dc_diag = { broadcasts: 0, writes: 0, writeErrs: 0, lastErr: null, history: [] };\n\n    // Broadcast helper. Re-assignment OK across re-renders; consumers read via globalThis lazily.\n    // Subscribers carry `closeOnTurnEnd` flag: POST /v1/prompt SSE wants close, /v1/stream doesn't.\n    globalThis.__dc_broadcast = function (name, data) {\n      let D = globalThis.__dc_diag;\n      D.broadcasts++;\n      let perSubResults = [];\n      let msg = \"event: \" + name + \"\\ndata: \" + JSON.stringify(data) + \"\\n\\n\";\n      let i = 0;\n      for (let s of globalThis.__dc_subscribers) {\n        let tag = s.tag || \"?\";\n        try {\n          let r = s.write(msg);\n          D.writes++;\n          perSubResults.push({ i, tag, ok: true, ret: r });\n        } catch (E) {\n          D.writeErrs++;\n          D.lastErr = String(E);\n          perSubResults.push({ i, tag, ok: false, err: String(E) });\n        }\n        if (s.closeOnTurnEnd && name === \"turn.end\") {\n          setTimeout(() => {\n            globalThis.__dc_subscribers.delete(s);\n            try { s.end(); } catch (_) {}\n          }, 10);\n        }\n        i++;\n      }\n      D.history.push({ ts: Date.now(), event: name, subs: perSubResults });\n      if (D.history.length > 50) D.history.shift();\n    };\n\n    let __dc_of = globalThis.fetch;\n    globalThis.fetch = async function (I, N) {\n      let U = typeof I === \"string\" ? I : (I && I.url) || \"\";\n      // Fire request_start BEFORE awaiting upstream — gives subscribers a\n      // signal that an Anthropic call is in flight before any byte returns.\n      // Critical for the SSE POST handler's slash-command-vs-API discriminator.\n      if (U.includes(\"api.anthropic.com\")) {\n        try { globalThis.__dc_broadcast && globalThis.__dc_broadcast(\"anthropic.request_start\", { url: U }); } catch (_) {}\n      }\n      let R = await __dc_of.call(this, I, N);\n      try {\n        if (!U.includes(\"api.anthropic.com\")) return R;\n        if (!R.body) return R;\n        let [A, B] = R.body.tee();\n        let M = new Response(A, { status: R.status, statusText: R.statusText, headers: R.headers });\n        (async () => {\n          let RD = B.getReader();\n          let DC = new TextDecoder();\n          let TX = \"\";\n          let lastStopReason = null;     // PER-CALL scope (advisor risk #1)\n          let lastScannedLen = 0;\n          try {\n            while (true) {\n              let { done: D, value: V } = await RD.read();\n              if (D) break;\n              let chunkText = DC.decode(V, { stream: true });\n              TX += chunkText;\n              // Per-chunk broadcast (raw passthrough — client parses SSE).\n              try {\n                globalThis.__dc_broadcast && globalThis.__dc_broadcast(\"anthropic.chunk\", { url: U, chunk: chunkText });\n              } catch (_) {}\n              // Scan accumulated TX with overlap so chunk-boundary splits don't miss (advisor risk #2).\n              let scanFrom = Math.max(0, lastScannedLen - 30);\n              let region = TX.slice(scanFrom);\n              let mm = region.match(/\"stop_reason\":\"([a-z_]+)\"/g);\n              if (mm) {\n                let last = mm[mm.length - 1];\n                lastStopReason = last.slice(15, -1);  // strip `\"stop_reason\":\"` (15 chars) and trailing `\"`\n              }\n              lastScannedLen = TX.length;\n            }\n            TX += DC.decode();\n          } catch (E) {\n            TX += \"\\n[dc-stream-error: \" + String(E) + \"]\";\n          }\n          let H = {};\n          for (let [K, V] of R.headers.entries()) H[K] = V;\n          globalThis.__dc_http_log.push({ ts: Date.now(), url: U, status: R.status, headers: H, body: TX });\n          if (globalThis.__dc_http_log.length > 200) globalThis.__dc_http_log.shift();\n          // Decide turn.end. Terminal stop_reason -> broadcast. tool_use/pause_turn -> stay open (next call coming).\n          if (lastStopReason && globalThis.__dc_TURN_END_REASONS.has(lastStopReason)) {\n            try {\n              globalThis.__dc_broadcast && globalThis.__dc_broadcast(\"turn.end\", { stop_reason: lastStopReason, source: \"stop_reason\", url: U });\n            } catch (_) {}\n          }\n        })();\n        return M;\n      } catch (E) { return R; }\n    };\n  }\n\n  // ========== Per-render: capture latest globals + dialog transition detection ==========\n  globalThis.__dc_submit = kCH;\n  globalThis.__dc_msgs = () => new Promise(r => R4(p => { r(p); return p; }));\n  globalThis.__dc_toolJSX = l6;\n  globalThis.__dc_setToolJSX = j6;\n  globalThis.__dc_appstate = () => { try { return AH.getState(); } catch (_) { return null; } };\n  globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache = globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache || new Map();\n\n  if (globalThis.__dc_last_l6 !== l6) {\n    let prevDid = globalThis.__dc_current_dialog_id;\n    globalThis.__dc_last_l6 = l6;\n    if (l6 != null && l6.jsx && l6.jsx.props) {\n      let did = \"dlg_\" + Date.now().toString(36) + \"_\" + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);\n      let t = l6.jsx.type;\n      let cn = t == null ? \"null\" : typeof t === \"string\" ? t : (t.displayName || t.name || \"anon-fn\");\n      let cbs = {};\n      for (let k of Object.keys(l6.jsx.props)) {\n        if (typeof l6.jsx.props[k] === \"function\") cbs[k] = l6.jsx.props[k];\n      }\n      globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache.set(did, { id: did, component: cn, callbacks: cbs, createdAt: Date.now() });\n      globalThis.__dc_current_dialog_id = did;\n      if (globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache.size > 10) {\n        let first = globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache.keys().next().value;\n        globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache.delete(first);\n      }\n      try {\n        globalThis.__dc_broadcast && globalThis.__dc_broadcast(\"dialog.opened\", { dialog_id: did, component: cn, propKeys: Object.keys(l6.jsx.props) });\n      } catch (_) {}\n    } else {\n      globalThis.__dc_current_dialog_id = null;\n      if (prevDid) {\n        try {\n          globalThis.__dc_broadcast && globalThis.__dc_broadcast(\"dialog.closed\", { dialog_id: prevDid });\n        } catch (_) {}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // ========== One-time install (HTTP server) ==========\n  if (globalThis.__dc_server) return;\n\n  let __dc_safe = (o, d, seen) => {\n    if (d > 6 || o == null) return o;\n    if (typeof o === \"function\") return \"[fn:\" + (o.name || \"anon\") + \"]\";\n    if (typeof o !== \"object\") return o;\n    if (seen.has(o)) return \"[circular]\";\n    seen.add(o);\n    if (Array.isArray(o)) return o.slice(0, 30).map(x => __dc_safe(x, d + 1, seen));\n    let r = {};\n    for (let k of Object.keys(o).slice(0, 60)) {\n      try { r[k] = __dc_safe(o[k], d + 1, seen); } catch (_) { r[k] = \"[err]\"; }\n    }\n    return r;\n  };\n  let __dc_jsx_meta = (j) => {\n    if (j == null || typeof j !== \"object\") return null;\n    let t = j.type;\n    let n = t == null ? \"null\" : typeof t === \"string\" ? t : (t.displayName || t.name || \"anon-fn\");\n    return { component: n, propKeys: j.props ? Object.keys(j.props) : [], propsSummary: __dc_safe(j.props, 0, new Set) };\n  };\n  let __dc_dump = (el) => {\n    if (el == null) return null;\n    return { wrapperKeys: Object.keys(el), isLocalJSXCommand: el.isLocalJSXCommand, showSpinner: el.showSpinner, shouldHidePromptInput: el.shouldHidePromptInput, dialog_id: globalThis.__dc_current_dialog_id, jsx: __dc_jsx_meta(el.jsx) };\n  };\n\n  try {\n    globalThis.__dc_server = require(\"node:http\").createServer(async (rq, rs) => {\n      // ----- GET /v1/diag — broadcast diagnostics -----\n      if (rq.method === \"GET\" && rq.url === \"/v1/diag\") {\n        rs.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n        let subs = [];\n        for (let s of globalThis.__dc_subscribers) subs.push({ tag: s.tag, closeOnTurnEnd: !!s.closeOnTurnEnd });\n        rs.end(JSON.stringify({ diag: globalThis.__dc_diag, subscribers: subs, subCount: globalThis.__dc_subscribers.size }, null, 2));\n        return;\n      }\n\n      // ----- GET /v1/state -----\n      if (rq.method === \"GET\" && rq.url === \"/v1/state\") {\n        let st = globalThis.__dc_appstate && globalThis.__dc_appstate();\n        let interesting = {};\n        if (st) {\n          for (let k of [\"elicitation\", \"toolPermissionContext\", \"activeOverlays\", \"pendingWorkerRequest\", \"pendingSandboxRequest\", \"pendingMemoryUpdates\", \"classifierApprovals\", \"channelPermissionCallbacks\", \"notifications\"]) {\n            try { interesting[k] = __dc_safe(st[k], 0, new Set); } catch (_) { interesting[k] = \"[err]\"; }\n          }\n        }\n        rs.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n        rs.end(JSON.stringify({ dialog: __dc_dump(globalThis.__dc_toolJSX), hasDialog: globalThis.__dc_toolJSX != null, appState: interesting }));\n        return;\n      }\n\n      // ----- POST /v1/answer -----\n      if (rq.method === \"POST\" && rq.url === \"/v1/answer\") {\n        let bd2 = \"\";\n        rq.on(\"data\", c => bd2 += c);\n        rq.on(\"end\", () => {\n          try {\n            let { callback: cb, args: ag = [], dialog_id: did = null } = JSON.parse(bd2 || \"{}\");\n            let snap = null;\n            if (did) {\n              snap = globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache && globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache.get(did);\n              if (!snap) {\n                rs.writeHead(410, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n                rs.end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"dialog_id not in cache\", dialog_id: did, available_ids: globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache ? [...globalThis.__dc_dialog_cache.keys()] : [] }));\n                return;\n              }\n            } else {\n              let cur = globalThis.__dc_toolJSX;\n              if (cur == null || !cur.jsx || !cur.jsx.props) {\n                rs.writeHead(409, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n                rs.end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"no dialog open\" }));\n                return;\n              }\n              let cbs = {};\n              for (let k of Object.keys(cur.jsx.props)) {\n                if (typeof cur.jsx.props[k] === \"function\") cbs[k] = cur.jsx.props[k];\n              }\n              snap = { id: globalThis.__dc_current_dialog_id, callbacks: cbs };\n            }\n            let fn = snap.callbacks[cb];\n            if (typeof fn !== \"function\") {\n              rs.writeHead(400, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n              rs.end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"callback not found\", available: Object.keys(snap.callbacks), dialog_id: snap.id }));\n              return;\n            }\n            let result;\n            try { result = fn.apply(null, ag); }\n            catch (e) {\n              rs.writeHead(500, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n              rs.end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"callback threw\", detail: String(e && e.stack || e), dialog_id: snap.id }));\n              return;\n            }\n            rs.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n            rs.end(JSON.stringify({ ok: true, returned: result == null ? null : String(result).slice(0, 200), dialog_id: snap.id }));\n          } catch (e) {\n            rs.writeHead(500, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n            rs.end(JSON.stringify({ error: String(e) }));\n          }\n        });\n        return;\n      }\n\n      // ----- GET /v1/stream — ambient SSE subscriber -----\n      if (rq.method === \"GET\" && rq.url === \"/v1/stream\") {\n        rs.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"text/event-stream\", \"cache-control\": \"no-cache\", \"connection\": \"keep-alive\", \"x-accel-buffering\": \"no\" });\n        rs.write(\":connected\\n\\n\");\n        let sub = { write: (m) => { try { rs.write(m); } catch (_) {} }, end: () => { try { rs.end(); } catch (_) {} }, closeOnTurnEnd: false, tag: \"ambient\" };\n        globalThis.__dc_subscribers.add(sub);\n        let ping = setInterval(() => { try { rs.write(\":ping\\n\\n\"); } catch (_) {} }, 15000);\n        let cleanup = () => { globalThis.__dc_subscribers.delete(sub); clearInterval(ping); };\n        rq.on(\"close\", cleanup);\n        rs.on(\"close\", cleanup);\n        return;\n      }\n\n      // ----- POST /v1/prompt -----\n      if (rq.method !== \"POST\" || rq.url !== \"/v1/prompt\") {\n        rs.writeHead(404);\n        rs.end();\n        return;\n      }\n      let bd = \"\";\n      rq.on(\"data\", c => bd += c);\n      rq.on(\"end\", async () => {\n        try {\n          let { prompt: pm, mode: md = \"prompt\", skipSlashCommands: ss = false } = JSON.parse(bd || \"{}\");\n          if (typeof pm !== \"string\" || !pm) {\n            rs.writeHead(400, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n            rs.end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"missing prompt\" }));\n            return;\n          }\n          if (!globalThis.__dc_submit) {\n            rs.writeHead(503, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n            rs.end(JSON.stringify({ error: \"submit not ready\" }));\n            return;\n          }\n          let uu = require(\"crypto\").randomUUID();\n          let acceptSSE = ((rq.headers[\"accept\"] || \"\") + \"\").indexOf(\"text/event-stream\") !== -1;\n\n          if (acceptSSE) {\n            // ---- SSE streaming path ----\n            // Two terminating signals:\n            //   1. PRIMARY: broadcast emits `event: turn.end` (from fetch wrap stop_reason\n            //      scan or own max_timeout/idle). closeOnTurnEnd=true asks broadcast helper\n            //      to schedule sub.end() right after writing turn.end.\n            //   2. FALLBACK (slash command path): submit promise resolved AND no\n            //      anthropic.request_start broadcast was observed for slashGraceMs since\n            //      handler start. Without this we'd hold the connection for max_timeout\n            //      on every /command. With it, slash commands close ~slashGraceMs after submit.\n            //\n            // We do NOT use http_log growth as the activity signal — kCH's submit promise\n            // resolves at ENQUEUE time (not turn-end), so submitDone+idle would fire\n            // before the first chunk arrives for API prompts. anthropic.request_start\n            // fires synchronously at fetch interception, before any response byte.\n            rs.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"text/event-stream\", \"cache-control\": \"no-cache\", \"connection\": \"keep-alive\", \"x-accel-buffering\": \"no\" });\n            let sawApiCall = false;\n            let sub = {\n              write: (m) => {\n                try { rs.write(m); } catch (_) {}\n                if (m.startsWith(\"event: anthropic.\")) sawApiCall = true;\n              },\n              end: () => { try { rs.end(); } catch (_) {} },\n              closeOnTurnEnd: true,\n              tag: \"post-sse:\" + uu.slice(0, 8),\n            };\n            globalThis.__dc_subscribers.add(sub);\n            let ping = setInterval(() => { try { rs.write(\":ping\\n\\n\"); } catch (_) {} }, 15000);\n            let teardown = () => { globalThis.__dc_subscribers.delete(sub); clearInterval(ping); try { rs.end(); } catch (_) {} };\n            // DO NOT subscribe to rq.on(\"close\") — under bun's node:http compat layer,\n            // rq.on(\"close\") fires shortly after rq.on(\"end\") for POST requests with\n            // bodies, NOT only when the client disconnects. Use rs.on(\"close\") which\n            // fires when the underlying response stream closes (true client disconnect).\n            rs.on(\"close\", () => { globalThis.__dc_subscribers.delete(sub); clearInterval(ping); });\n\n            // Manual rs.write for turn.start — bypasses sub.write so it doesn't count as anthropic activity.\n            try { rs.write(\"event: turn.start\\ndata: \" + JSON.stringify({ turn_uuid: uu, prompt: pm }) + \"\\n\\n\"); } catch (_) {}\n\n            let submitDone = false;\n            let submitP = globalThis.__dc_submit([{ value: pm, preExpansionValue: pm, mode: md, pastedContents: void 0, skipSlashCommands: ss, uuid: uu }]);\n            submitP.catch(() => {});\n            submitP.then(() => { submitDone = true; });\n\n            let slashGraceMs = Number(process.env.DC_SLASH_GRACE_MS || 1500);\n            let maxMs = Number(process.env.DC_MAX_MS || 120000);\n            let started = Date.now();\n            let watcher = setInterval(() => {\n              if (!globalThis.__dc_subscribers.has(sub)) { clearInterval(watcher); return; }\n              if (Date.now() - started > maxMs) {\n                clearInterval(watcher);\n                try { sub.write(\"event: turn.end\\ndata: \" + JSON.stringify({ turn_uuid: uu, stop_reason: null, source: \"max_timeout\" }) + \"\\n\\n\"); } catch (_) {}\n                teardown();\n                return;\n              }\n              if (submitDone && !sawApiCall && Date.now() - started > slashGraceMs) {\n                // Slash-command path: submit settled, no Anthropic call ever fired.\n                clearInterval(watcher);\n                try { sub.write(\"event: turn.end\\ndata: \" + JSON.stringify({ turn_uuid: uu, stop_reason: null, source: \"idle_fallback\" }) + \"\\n\\n\"); } catch (_) {}\n                teardown();\n              }\n              // If sawApiCall, primary signal (turn.end via broadcast) closes us — or max_timeout.\n            }, 100);\n            return;\n          }\n\n          // ---- Blocking JSON path (unchanged) ----\n          let bf = (await globalThis.__dc_msgs()).length;\n          let httpBf = globalThis.__dc_http_log.length;\n          let submitP = globalThis.__dc_submit([{ value: pm, preExpansionValue: pm, mode: md, pastedContents: void 0, skipSlashCommands: ss, uuid: uu }]);\n          submitP.catch(() => {});\n          let submitDone = false;\n          submitP.then(() => { submitDone = true; });\n          let stableMs = Number(process.env.DC_STABLE_MS || 800);\n          let maxMs = Number(process.env.DC_MAX_MS || 120000);\n          let pollMs = 100;\n          let lastLen = (await globalThis.__dc_msgs()).length;\n          let stableSince = Date.now();\n          let started = Date.now();\n          while (Date.now() - started < maxMs) {\n            await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, pollMs));\n            if (globalThis.__dc_toolJSX != null) break;\n            let cur = (await globalThis.__dc_msgs()).length;\n            if (cur !== lastLen) { lastLen = cur; stableSince = Date.now(); continue; }\n            if (submitDone && Date.now() - stableSince >= stableMs) break;\n          }\n          let af = await globalThis.__dc_msgs();\n          let ad = af.slice(bf);\n          let raw = ad.map(m => {\n            try { return { type: m.type, role: m.message && m.message.role, content: m.message && m.message.content, uuid: m.uuid, toolUseID: m.toolUseID, toolUseResult: m.toolUseResult, isMeta: m.isMeta, timestamp: m.timestamp }; }\n            catch (_) { return null; }\n          }).filter(Boolean);\n          rs.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n          let httpResp = globalThis.__dc_http_log.slice(httpBf);\n          rs.end(JSON.stringify({ httpResponses: httpResp, uuid: uu, added: ad.length, messages: raw, waitedMs: Date.now() - started, pending: globalThis.__dc_toolJSX != null ? __dc_dump(globalThis.__dc_toolJSX) : null }));\n        } catch (e) {\n          rs.writeHead(500, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n          rs.end(JSON.stringify({ error: String(e && e.stack || e) }));\n        }\n      });\n    }).listen(Number(process.env.DC_PORT || 47291), \"127.0.0.1\");\n  } catch (e) {\n    globalThis.__dc_server = null;\n  }\n}, [kCH, R4, l6]);\n"
    }
  ]
}
